# netsurf: downloads to ux0:download/ (Vita frontend)
#
# A response the engine does not display (a VPK, a zip, <a download>) is
# saved to ux0:download/ -- the folder VitaShell and other file managers
# show -- under its Content-Disposition or URL name, made safe for the
# card and unique ("name (2).ext" if taken). Progress and the result go to
# the on-screen message line and log.txt; a failed download removes its
# partial file. The home page lists what is on the card.
#
# New vita/download.c|h (a gui_download_table): the engine's
# browser_window_download() drives .create/.data/.error/.done. The message
# line is vita_show_message() (vita/main.c, the old diag-only path),
# registered through the frontend table as .download. interact.c gains a
# C_DOWNLOAD step: open IN-download.html, tap the <a download> box, and
# check ux0:download/vita-test.bin is 1024 bytes and starts with its
# magic string (tools/run-vita-sim.sh re-checks it byte for byte against
# the bundled testpages target). Verified in the sim: the saved file is
# byte-identical to testpages/IN-download-target.bin.
#
